# Antigravity Agent Rules

## General Guidelines
- Be concise and to the point.
- Ask clarifying questions when requirements are ambiguous.
- Prioritize correct and working code over premature optimization.

## Coding Standards
- Write clean, maintainable, and well-document code.
- Always include helpful comments for complex logic.
- Follow the existing code style and conventions of the workspace (e.g., naming conventions, formatting).
- Ensure error handling is robust and logs are informative.

## Project Context
- **MUST READ**: Always refer to `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for understanding the end-to-end architecture, service boundaries, and data flow of the CTO Dashboard project before suggesting major architectural changes or when you need overall context.

## Communication
- Provide clear explanations for architectural or design decisions.
- Format code blocks with the appropriate language tags.
